  "content_type": "narrative",
  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "أَبِي رَحِمَهُ اللَّهُ، قَالَ: حَدَّثَنَا أَحْمَدُ بْنُ إِدْرِيسَ وَمُحَمَّدُ بْنُ يَحْيَى الْعَطَّارُ، عَنِ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ أَحْمَدَ، عَنِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ بْنِ هَاشِمٍ، عَنِ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ حَمَّادٍ، عَنِ الْحَسَنِ بْنِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ، عَنِ يُونُسَ بْنِ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ، عَنْ هِشَامَ بْنِ الْحَكَمِ، عَنْ جَاثَلِيقٍ مِنْ جَثَالِقَةِ النَّصَارَى يُقَالُ لَهُ: بُرَيْهَةُ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "My father (peace be upon him), may Allah have mercy on him, said: Ahmad ibn Idris and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Attar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ahmad, from Ibrahim ibn Hashim, from Muhammad ibn Hammad, from al-Hasan ibn Ibrahim, from Yunus ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hisham ibn al-Hakam, from a Catholicos (primate) among the Catholici of the Christians, who was called Burayhah,"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَدْ مَكَثَ جَاثَلِيقَ النَّصْرَانِيَّةَ سَبْعِينَ سَنَةً، وَكَانَ يَطْلُبُ الْإِسْلَامَ وَيَطْلُبُ مَنْ يُحَاجُّهُ عَلَيْهِ مِمَّنْ يَقْرَأُ كُتُبَهُ وَيَعْرِفُ الْمَسِيحَ بِصِفَاتِهِ وَدَلَائِلِهِ وَآيَاتِهِ، قَالَ: وَعُرِفَ بِذَلِكَ حَتَّى اشْتَهَرَ فِي النَّصَارَى وَالْمُسْلِمِينَ وَالْيَهُودَ وَالْمَجُوسَ حَتَّى افْتَخَرَتْ بِهِ النَّصَارَى وَقَالَتْ: لَوْ لَا بُرَيْهَةُ فِي دِينِ النَّصْرَانِيَّةِ لَأَجْزَأَنَا، وَكَانَ طَالِبًا لِلْحَقِّ وَالْإِسْلَامِ مَعَ ذَلِكَ، وَكَانَتْ مَعَهُ امْرَأَةٌ تَخْدُمُهُ، طَالَ مَكَثُهَا مَعَهُ، وَكَانَ يُسِرُّ إِلَيْهَا ضَعْفَ النَّصْرَانِيَّةِ وَضَعْفَ حُجَّتِهَا،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "had remained as Catholicos of Christianity for seventy years. He used to seek Islam and seek someone to debate him regarding it from among those who read his books and knew the Messiah by his attributes, proofs, and signs. He says: He became known for this until he became famous among the Christians, Muslims, Jews, and Zoroastrians. The Christians boasted about him and said: 'If there were no one in the Christian faith except Burayhah, that would suffice us.' He was a seeker of the truth and Islam at the same time. A woman served him, and she had been with him for a long time. He would whisper to her about the weakness of Christianity and the weakness of its proofs."
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ: فَعَرَفْتُ ذَلِكَ مِنْهُ، فَضَرَبَ بُرَيْهَةُ الْأَمْرَ ظَهْرًا لِبَطْنٍ وَأَقْبَلَ يَسْأَلُ فُرَقَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ وَالْمُخْتَلِفِينَ فِي الْإِسْلَامِ مِنْ أَعْلَمِكُمْ؟ وَأَقْبَلَ يَسْأَلُ عَنْ أَئِمَّةِ الْمُسْلِمِينَ وَعَنْ صَلِحَائِهِمْ وَعُلَمَائِهِمْ، وَأَهْلِ الْحُجَى مِنْهُمْ، وَكَانَ يَسْتَقْرِئُ فِرْقَةً فِرْقَةً لَا يَجِدُ عِنْدَ الْقَوْمِ شَيْئًا، وَقَالَ: لَوْ كَانَتْ أَئِمَّتُكُمْ أَئِمَّةً عَلَى الْحَقِّ لَكَانَ عِنْدَكُمْ بَعْضُ الْحَقِّ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "I came to know that from him. So Burayhah put the matter behind him and turned to ask the various sects of Muslims and those who differed in Islam: 'Who is the most knowledgeable among you?' He turned to ask about the Imams of the Muslims, their pious ones, their scholars, and their leading intellectuals. He examined every sect and found nothing with the people. He said: 'If your Imams were Imams upon the truth, there would be some truth with you.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "فَوُصِفَتْ لَهُ الشِّيعَةُ، وَوُصِفَ لَهُ هِشَامُ بْنُ الْحَكَمِ، فَقَالَ يُونُسُ بْنُ عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ: قَالَ لِي هِشَامٌ: بَيْنَمَا أَنَا عَلَى دَكَّانِي عَلَى بَابِ الْكَرْخِ جَالِسًا وَعِنْدِي قَوْمٌ يَقْرَؤُونَ عَلَيَّ الْقُرْآنَ إِذَا أَنَا بِفَوْجِ النَّصَارَى مَعَهُ مَا بَيْنَ الْقِسِّيسِينَ إِلَى غَيْرِهِمْ نَحْوَ مِنْ مِائَةِ رَجُلٍ عَلَيْهِمُ السَّوَادُ وَالْبَرَانِسُ، وَالْجَاثَلِيقُ الْأَكْبَرُ فِيهِمْ بُرَيْهَةُ حَتَّى نَزَلُوا حَوْلَ دَكَّانِي،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "The Shi'ites were described to him, and Hisham ibn al-Hakam was described to him. Yunus ibn Abd al-Rahman said: Hisham said to me: 'While I was sitting in my shop at the door of al-Karkh, with a group of people reciting the Quran to me, suddenly a group of Christians came, from priests to others, about a hundred men, wearing black and chasubles, and the Great Catholicos among them was Burayhah, until they settled around my shop.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "وَجَعَلَ لِبُرَيْهَةَ كُرْسِيًّا يَجْلِسُ عَلَيْهِ، فَقَامَتِ الْأَسَاقِفَةُ وَالرَّهْبَانَةُ عَلَى عَصِيهِمْ، وَعَلَى رُءُوسِهِمْ بَرَانِسُهُمْ، فَقَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: مَا بَقِيَ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ أَحَدٌ مِمَّنْ يُذْكَرُ بِالْعِلْمِ بِالْكَلَامِ إِلَّا وَقَدْ نَازَرْتُهُ فِي النَّصْرَانِيَّةِ فَمَا عِنْدَهُمْ شَيْءٌ، وَقَدْ جِئْتُ أَنَا أُحَاجُّكَ فِي الْإِسْلَامِ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "They placed a chair for Burayhah to sit on. The bishops and monks stood leaning on their staffs, with their chasubles on their heads. Burayhah said: 'No one from the Muslims who is known for knowledge of theology remains whom I have not debated regarding Christianity, and they had nothing with them. I have come to debate you regarding Islam.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ: فَضَحِكَ هِشَامٌ فَقَالَ: يَا بُرَيْهَةُ إِنْ كُنْتَ تُرِيدُ مِنِّي آيَاتٍ كَآيَاتِ الْمَسِيحِ فَلَسْتُ أَنَا بِالْمَسِيحِ وَلَا مِثْلَهُ وَلَا أَدَانِيَهُ، ذَاكَ رُوحٌ طَيِّبَةٌ خَمِيصَةٌ مُرْتَفِعَةٌ، آيَاتُهُ ظَاهِرَةٌ، وَعَلَامَاتُهُ قَائِمَةٌ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "He says: Hisham laughed and said: 'O Burayhah! If you expect from me signs like the signs of the Messiah, I am not the Messiah, nor like him, nor close to him. That is a pure spirit, humble yet exalted. His signs are manifest, and his marks are established.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: فَأَعْجَبَنِي الْكَلَامُ وَالْوَصْفُ، قَالَ هِشَامٌ: إِنْ أَرَدْتَ الْحُجَّاجَ فَهَهُنَا، قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: نَعَمْ، فَإِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ مَا نِسْبَةُ نَبِيِّكَ هَذَا مِنَ الْمَسِيحِ نِسْبَةَ الْأَبْدَانِ؟",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Burayhah said: 'I was pleased with the speech and the description.' Hisham said: 'If you want to argue, then go ahead.' Burayhah said: 'Yes, for I ask you: What is the physical relationship of this Prophet of yours to the Messiah?'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ هِشَامٌ: ابْنُ عَمِّ جَدِّهِ (لِأُمِّهِ) لِأَنَّهُ مِنْ وَلَدِ إِسْحَاقَ وَمُحَمَّدٌ مِنْ وَلَدِ إِسْمَاعِيلَ، قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: وَكَيْفَ تَنْسِبُهُ إِلَى أَبِيهِ؟",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Hisham said: 'He is the son of his maternal grandfather, because he is from the offspring of Isaac, and Muhammad is from the offspring of Ishmael.' Burayhah said: 'And how do you relate him to his father?'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ هِشَامٌ: إِنْ أَرَدْتَ نَسَبَهُ عِنْدَنَا أَخْبَرْتُكَ، وَإِنْ أَرَدْتَ نَسَبَهُ عِنْدَنَا أَخْبَرْتُكَ، قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: أُرِيدُ نَسَبَهُ عِنْدَنَا، وَظَنَنْتُ أَنَّهُ إِذَا نَسَبَهُ نَسَبْنَا أَغْلَبَهُ، قُلْتُ: فَانْسَبْهُ بِالنِّسْبَةِ الَّتِي نَنْسَبُهُ بِهَا،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Hisham said: 'If you want his lineage according to us, I will inform you. If you want his lineage according to us, I will inform you.' Burayhah said: 'I want his lineage according to us.' I thought that if he described his lineage according to us, I would overpower him. I said: 'Describe his lineage with the lineage by which we relate him.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ هِشَامٌ: نَعَمْ، تَقُولُونَ: إِنَّهُ قَدِيمٌ مِنْ قَدِيمٍ، فَأَيُّهُمَا الْأَبُ وَأَيُّهُمَا الْابْنُ؟",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Hisham said: 'Yes. You say: He is eternal from the Eternal. Then which one is the Father and which one is the Son?'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: الَّذِي نَزَلَ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ الْابْنُ، قَالَ هِشَامٌ: الَّذِي نَزَلَ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ الْأَبُ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Burayhah said: 'He who descended to the earth is the Son.' Hisham said: 'He who descended to the earth is the Father.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: الْابْنُ رَسُولُ الْأَبِ، قَالَ هِشَامٌ: إِنَّ الْأَبَ أَحْكَمُ مِنَ الْابْنِ لِأَنَّ الْخَلْقَ خَلَقَ الْأَبُ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Burayhah said: 'The Son is the messenger of the Father.' Hisham said: 'Verily, the Father is wiser than the Son, because the Father created the creation.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: إِنَّ الْخَلْقَ خَلَقَ الْأَبُ وَخَلَقَ الْابْنُ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Burayhah said: 'Verily, the Father created and the Son created.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ هِشَامٌ: مَا مَنَعَهُمَا أَنْ يَنْزِلَا جَمِيعًا كَمَا خُلِقَا إِذَا اشْتَرَكَا؟",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Hisham said: 'What prevented them from descending together as they were created, if they share in creation?'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: كَيْفَ يَشْتَرِكَانِ وَهُمَا شَيْءٌ وَاحِدٌ، إِنَّمَا يَفْتَرِقَانِ بِالِاسْمِ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Burayhah said: 'How can they share while they are one thing? They differ only by name.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ هِشَامٌ: إِنَّمَا يَجْتَمِعَانِ بِالِاسْمِ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Hisham said: 'They unite only by name.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: جَهْلُ هَذَا الْكَلَامِ، قَالَ هِشَامٌ: عُرْفُ هَذَا الْكَلَامِ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Burayhah said: 'This speech is unknown (to us).' Hisham said: 'This speech is known.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: إِنَّ الْابْنَ مُتَّصِلٌ بِالْأَبِ، قَالَ هِشَامٌ: إِنَّ الْابْنَ مُنْفَصِلٌ مِنَ الْأَبِ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Burayhah said: 'Verily, the Son is connected to the Father.' Hisham said: 'Verily, the Son is separate from the Father.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: هَذَا خِلَافُ مَا يَعْقِلُهُ النَّاسُ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Burayhah said: 'This is contrary to what people understand.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ هِشَامٌ: إِنْ كَانَ مَا يَعْقِلُهُ النَّاسُ شَاهِدًا لَنَا وَعَلَيْنَا فَقَدْ غَلَبْتُكَ، لِأَنَّ الْأَبَ كَانَ وَلَمْ يَكُنِ الْابْنُ، فَتَقُولُ: هَكَذَا يَا بُرَيْهَةُ؟",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Hisham said: 'If what people understand is a witness for us and against us, then I have overcome you, because the Father was when the Son was not. So you say: Like this, O Burayhah?'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ: مَا أَقُولُ: هَكَذَا،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "He said: 'I do not say: Like this.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ: فَلِمَ اسْتَشْهَدْتَ قَوْمًا لَا تَقْبَلُ شَهَادَتَهُمْ لِنَفْسِكَ؟",
      "translations": {
        "en": "He said: 'Then why did you call as witnesses people whose testimony you do not accept for yourself?'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: إِنَّ الْأَبَ اسْمٌ وَالِابْنُ اسْمٌ يُقَدَّرُ بِهِ الْقَدِيمُ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Burayhah said: 'Verily, the Father is a name and the Son is a name, by which the Eternal is designated.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ هِشَامٌ: الْاسْمَانِ قَدِيمَانِ كَقَدَمِ الْأَبِ وَالِابْنِ؟",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Hisham said: 'Are the two names eternal like the eternity of the Father and the Son?'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: لَا، وَلَكِنَّ الْأَسْمَاءَ مُحْدَثَةٌ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Burayhah said: 'No, but the names are originated (created).'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ: فَقَدْ جَعَلْتَ الْأَبَ ابْنًا وَالِابْنَ أَبًا، إِنْ كَانَ الْابْنُ أَحْدَثَ هَذِهِ الْأَسْمَاءَ دُونَ الْأَبِ فَهُوَ الْأَبُ، وَإِنْ كَانَ الْأَبُ أَحْدَثَ هَذِهِ الْأَسْمَاءَ دُونَ الْابْنِ فَهُوَ الْأَبُ وَالِابْنُ أَبٌ، وَلَيْسَ هَهُنَا ابْنٌ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "He said: 'So you have made the Father a son and the son a father. If the Son originated these names without the Father, then he is the Father. And if the Father originated these names without the Son, then he is the Father and the son is a father. And there is no son here.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ بُرَيْهَةُ: إِنَّ الْابْنَ اسْمٌ لِلرُّوحِ حِينَ نَزَلَتْ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ،",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Burayhah said: 'Verily, the Son is a name for the Spirit when it descended to the earth.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قَالَ هِشَامٌ: فَحِينَ لَمْ تَنْزِلْ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ فَاسْمُهَا مَا هُوَ؟",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Hisham said: 'So when it did not descend to the earth, what is its name?'"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
